# An operator we do not have says so, instead of quietly widening the search.
#
# `is:thinking` reads like it should work — puffin has it — but a thinking row
# has no highlight path: find skips it in collect_matches and paint_query_for
# together, so the operator could only ever answer "no matches", which is the
# lying tally the counting rule exists to prevent. (This note used to say the
# adapter folds a thinking block into the assistant text run so nothing
# distinguishes it once stored. That has not been true since reasoning became
# its own folded row — http_client.cpp sets `subtitle` from the block type and
# agentcloud_client.cpp sets "thinking" outright. See docs/SEARCH.md S11.)
# Treating an unknown operator as plain text would search for the literal
# "is:thinking" and report a tally for a question nobody asked. The bar names
# the operators that do exist instead, and finds nothing until the query is
# one of them.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["r1"],"active_tab":"r1","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_FIND_DEMO='backoff is:thinking' HANABI_FIND_AUDIT=1

expect_text "Try: is:user, is:assistant, has:tool, state:failed"
expect_text "no matches"

# Nothing counted, so nothing painted.
wait_frames 6
expect_text "bands 0"
